       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it looks like a dosing error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Doses above the maximum raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. A single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum of about 1000 mg per dose.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg per dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me and add a note with the rationale. I'd want that confirmed before I submit it."
